{
  format: 1
  name: install-move-from-stored-state-invalid
  suite: static
  spec: ["#modules", "§13.16", "§8.5"]
  note: '''
    §13.16 makes `<-` the install operator, which means the §8.5 move rule has to
    admit a source that is not a local binding. It admits exactly one: a value
    that types as `module`. That narrowness is the guard, and this case is the
    guard's test.

    The attack is a move out of ORDINARY stored state into a module slot — a row
    of a plain collection, where the author expected `<-` to "just work" because
    it works one line above with `unpack(@package)`. Nothing in the language can
    leave a stored row moved-from (§8.5: the move consumes its source), and a row
    is not a module, so there is no reading under which this installs anything.
    Admitting it would mean either copying under a move spelling or staging
    nothing at all while the program reports success.

    It is a LOAD error, not a runtime one: the source's type is known statically,
    so the mistake never has to reach a transition.
  '''

  package: {
    $liasse: 1
    $app: "t.modinstall.badsource@1.0.0"
    $model: {
      archive: { $key: "id", id: "text" }
      companies: {
        $key: "id"
        id: "text"
        modules: { $modules: {} }
      }
      $mut: {
        "provision({ company: text, name: text, from: text })": [
          ".companies[@company].modules[@name] <- .archive[@from]"
        ]
      }
    }
    $data: { companies: { acme: {} } }
  }

  expect: { outcome: invalid, violates: ["§8.5"] }
}
